---
import "./tl-styles.css";
---
<!-- PICAB Accreditation -->
        <section class="ascii-white-sec" id="tl-picab">
          <div class="ascii-container">
            <div class="tl-bento" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
              <div class="ascii-white-card gold-accent tl-span-4 col-4">
                <div class="ascii-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:6px;">EFFECTIVE DATE • STA. MESA, MANILA</div>
                <div
                  style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-maroon);line-height:1.15;margin-bottom:6px;">
                  July 25, 2026</div>
                <p style="font-size:0.86rem;color:#4B5563;margin:0;">Granted under the <strong>Computer Science Program
                    Criteria</strong>, confirming full compliance with established national computing education
                  standards.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="ascii-white-card gold-accent tl-span-4 col-4">
                <div class="ascii-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:6px;">NEXT COMPREHENSIVE REVIEW</div>
                <div
                  style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-maroon);line-height:1.15;margin-bottom:6px;">
                  Cycle 2031–2032</div>
                <p style="font-size:0.86rem;color:#4B5563;margin:0;">Accreditation remains in effect through the next
                  scheduled comprehensive evaluation in <strong>Accreditation Cycle 2031–2032</strong>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="ascii-white-card gold-accent tl-span-4 col-4">
                <div class="ascii-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:6px;">ACCREDITING BODY</div>
                <div
                  style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--color-maroon);line-height:1.15;margin-bottom:6px;">
                  PICAB / PCS</div>
                <p style="font-size:0.86rem;color:#4B5563;margin:0;">Established under the <strong>Philippine Computer
                    Society (PCS)</strong> as an independent accreditation board for computing and IT degree programs.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tl-bento" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
              <div class="ascii-soft-card tl-span-6 col-6">
                <div class="ascii-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:6px;">EXTERNAL QUALITY ASSURANCE SCOPE</div>
                <h3>Program Evaluation Dimensions</h3>
                <p>PICAB’s objective evaluation encompasses Program Educational Objectives (PEOs), Student Outcomes
                  (SOs),
                  curriculum design and implementation, faculty qualifications and development, instructional facilities
                  and resources, industry-academe linkages, and assessment of student learning.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="ascii-soft-card tl-span-6 col-6">
                <div class="ascii-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:6px;">CONTINUOUS QUALITY IMPROVEMENT</div>
                <h3>Actionable Accreditation Feedback Loop</h3>
                <p>Findings, observations, and recommendations from the PICAB evaluation guide ongoing curriculum
                  enhancements, syllabus and IM refinement, SO assessment strengthening, and instructional facility
                  upgrades in coordination with College and University offices.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div style="display:flex;justify-content:flex-start;">
              <a class="btn-drive"
                href="https://philippinecomputersociety.org/polytechnic-university-of-the-philippines-sta-mesa-manila-campus/"
                target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Official PCS / PICAB Accreditation Record ↗</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
